{
  "name": "The Complete Recruiter Sourcing System - Candidate Verification & Enrichment (LinkFinder AI)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Your FIRST action, before writing any response, must be a tool call. Do not output any text or a final answer until you have completed every applicable step below and actually called the required tools. A response with mostly blank fields, without having called Find Person's LinkedIn URL (or Reverse Email to LinkedIn URL) first, is a failure — go back and call it now if you haven't yet.\n\nHere is one candidate row from a recruiting pipeline. The candidate applied claiming the title and company below (resume data, may be outdated). Your job is to verify their current real-world status and find every piece of information you can about them using your LinkFinder AI tools — use the fewest tool calls necessary, don't call a tool for data already present, and don't call a tool if you have no way to get its required input yet.\n\nCandidate data (from application/resume, may be stale):\nfull_name: {{ $json.full_name }}\nresume_title: {{ $json.job }}\nresume_company: {{ $json.company_name }}\nlinkedin_url: {{ $json.linkedin_url }}\nemail: {{ $json.email }}\nphone: {{ $json.phone }}\nlocation: {{ $json.location }}\nabout: {{ $json.about }}\ndomain: {{ $json.domain }}\ncompany_linkedin: {{ $json.company_linkedin }}\neducation: {{ $json.education }}\nexperience: {{ $json.experiences }}\n\nExecute these steps in order, actually calling the tool at each step that applies — do not skip ahead or summarize without calling them:\n1. linkedin_url is blank and email is blank, but full_name and resume_company are both present → call Find Person's LinkedIn URL now with \"{{ $json.full_name }} {{ $json.company_name }}\".\n2. Once you have a linkedin_url from step 1: call Get Full LinkedIn Profile Info with it. This returns a job_id/poll_url. Call Check Job Status. If status is \"processing\", call Wait 60 Seconds, then Check Job Status again. Repeat until status is \"done\". Do not proceed until you have the actual result.\n3. From that result, extract current_title, current_company, location, headline, about, education, and experience — only for whichever of these are still blank above. The education field should list each degree/school found (institution, degree, field of study, years if available). The experience field should list each past role found (company, title, date range if available) — this is very important recruiting data, do not skip it even if it makes the response longer.\n4. Compare current_title/current_company against resume_title/resume_company. Set employment_match to \"Match\",",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a recruiting operations agent. Given a candidate's resume-claimed employment info, you verify their real current status and find every available piece of information about them and their current company using LinkFinder AI tools. Be precise about employment_match — recruiters make outreach decisions based on this, so don't call it a \"Match\" unless the scraped data genuinely confirms it, and don't call it a \"Mismatch\" on thin evidence; use \"Unknown\" whenever the evidence is ambiguous. Always attempt every enrichment field listed in the task (contact info, location, headline, about, current company details) rather than stopping once employment status is confirmed. Every tool call costs 1 credit even on a miss, so don't call a tool for data you already have and don't call a tool whose required input is still missing. Never fabricate names, titles, companies, emails, phone numbers, or any other field — if something can't be found, leave it blank."
        }
      },
